---
import MainLayout from "../layouts/main.astro";
---

<style>
  hr {
    margin: 2rem 0;
    border: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
  }

  article {
    margin-bottom: 128px;
  }

  .project {
    margin: 1px;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 64px 1fr;
    align-items: center;
    column-gap: 8px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    background-color: #fff;
    border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
    padding: 8px;
    font-size: 14px;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: inherit;
    transition: all 0.4s ease-in-out;

    &:hover {
      box-shadow: 0 1px 1px 1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);
    }
  }

  .project .info {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    row-gap: 2px;
  }

  li > p:first-of-type {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
</style>
<MainLayout>
  <h1>Hello, Linear</h1>
  <article>
    <p>A week ago marked 4 years of happy usage of your wonderful product.</p>
    <img
      width="100%"
      src="/images/linear-first-letter.png"
      alt="Linear first letter"
    />
    <p>
      It was love at first sight. I liked the clean and simple design, the idea
      of the app, and the attention to detail. It was Linear that taught me that
      when you move the cursor to the submenu, you need to take into account its
      path and not activate other menu items along the way. I’ve never thought
      about that kind of adjustment for better UX. I haven’t dreamed to join the
      team at that time, but I decided that I want to strive to the same level
      of care about the end user that you guys have.
    </p>
    <p>
      The stars aligned in such a way that I’m looking for a job at exactly the
      same time you have a position. I know that you have incredibly high
      standards, but I would like to try to tell a little about myself and see
      if I can fit those standards.
    </p>
    <hr />
    <p>
      I’m a frontend engineer with over 10 years of experience. I love to code
      and design things; I do this even in my free time.
    </p>
    <p>
      For example, I’m building an open-source rich text editor for my pet
      project. It is still in it’s early stage, but it gets better every week:
    </p>
    <a
      href="https://use-kona.github.io/editor/"
      target="_blank"
      class="project"
    >
      <img width="64px" src="/images/editor.png" alt="@use-kona/editor logo" />
      <div class="info">
        <strong>@use-kona/editor</strong>
        <span>Rich text editor based on Slate.js library</span>
      </div>
    </a>
    <p>
      A few lines about my pet project. I’m building it for the last 5 years
      with React, Typescript, Apollo GraphQL and Fastify. The UI is also built
      by me - I rarely use any 3rd party libraries.
    </p>
    <a
      href="https://use-kona.github.io/editor/"
      target="_blank"
      class="project"
    >
      <img width="64px" src="/icons/kona.svg" alt="@use-kona/editor logo" />
      <div class="info">
        <strong>Kona Calendar</strong>
        <span>Task management app with a built-in calendar</span>
      </div>
    </a>
    <p>What else can I do:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>I've been using React and TypeScript for more than 5 years</li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</MainLayout>
